WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.666
That is the damaged Chernobyl nuclear reactor.

00:00:03.666 --> 00:00:06.660
In 1986, after the accident it was encased in

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.087
the sarcophagus that you can see now

00:00:09.087 --> 00:00:12.000
but it's&nbsp;weathering and cracking and needs to be replaced

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:17.640
So they're building a new confinement structure&nbsp;
over here. They can't build it above the old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.620
sarcophagus because the levels of radiation are&nbsp;
still too high

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:25.000
so they'll have to slide the whole&nbsp;structure across.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.260
It'll cost billions of dollars&nbsp;
and this structure will last a hundred years.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:37.200
And that is only a temporary solution&nbsp;
because the half-life of uranium-238&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:44.340
is four and a half billion years. It's&nbsp;
the same as the lifetime of the Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:53.100
So in five billion years when all life has ceased&nbsp;
on this planet and the Sun is engulfing the Earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:59.025
only half of the uranium which is still in&nbsp;
that sarcophagus will have decayed away.

